# Claude Code. Local agent state stays out of the repo; SHARED slash commands
# are tracked one file at a time. The allowlist is per-file on purpose: a
# directory-level carve-out would also surface personal commands kept in
# .claude/commands/ as untracked, which is how a private file reaches a public
# repo by accident. Add one `!` line per command you mean to share.
# (`.claude/*`, not `.claude/`, because git cannot re-include anything under an
# excluded DIRECTORY, only under an excluded glob of its children.)
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
.claude/commands/*
!.claude/commands/thalia-review.md

# Env
.env
.env.local

# Job search (private, local-only). The tooling (skills.yaml + scripts +
# templates) is tracked; the real targets, contacts, and generated packets
# live here and must never reach this public repo.
/jobsearch/
